    "The small-workspace sorted wide-string fixture still uses singleton records and retains more decode memory than dictionary gathering; merge fan-in and block budgets remain unchanged.",
    "Wide spilled join allocation counts do not improve against the prior baseline; singleton input borrowing avoids needless lease ownership, but this fixture does not establish an allocation win.",
    "Remote catalog index publication, complete coverage selection, and materialization substitution remain unimplemented; these native measurements do not establish remote index serving."
